<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sharahbil Ya'fur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sharahbil Ya'fur was a king of Himyar in south <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> in the mid-5th century, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abikarib-asad">Abikarib As'ad</a>. A long inscription records his major repairs to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marib-dam">Marib Dam</a> in the 450s, after a breach. He continued his father's monotheist cult of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rahmanan">Rahmanan</a> and the Himyarite claim over the tribes of central Arabia.</p></div>
